WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.984
Hello, I'm Camille.

2
00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:05.782
Today, I'll show you how to spot a fake delivery text.

3
00:00:06.482 --> 00:00:08.282
Here is a typical message.

4
00:00:08.632 --> 00:00:11.584
First clue: it comes from an ordinary phone number.

5
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:18.670
Second clue: you're asked for a small sum. It's bait to get your card number.

6
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.500
Third clue: the link doesn't lead to the carrier's official website.

7
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.664
The right reflex?

8
00:00:25.014 --> 00:00:26.542
Never click the link.

9
00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:31.188
If you're expecting a parcel, check directly on the carrier's official website.

10
00:00:31.538 --> 00:00:37.098
And report the message by forwarding it, free of charge, to 7726, in the UK and the US.

11
00:00:37.798 --> 00:00:39.070
Already clicked?

12
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.804
If you entered your bank card details, block your card immediately.

13
00:00:43.154 --> 00:00:45.610
Then keep a close eye on your accounts.

14
00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:49.086
Remember: distrust is the mother of safety.

15
00:00:49.436 --> 00:00:53.100
That was Camille, for Prometis. See you soon!
